  "problem": "Simplify the following sentence: \"$x$ is odd and it is an odd number, or $x$ is odd or it is a prime number.\"",
  "worked_solution": "First, we simplify the phrase \"$x$ is odd and it is an odd number\" to just \"$x$ is odd.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$x$ is odd, or $x$ is odd or it is a prime number.\"\n\nThen, using the associative law, we can move the comma in the sentence:\n\n\"$x$ is odd or $x$ is odd, or it is a prime number.\"\n\nNow, we simplify the phrase \"$x$ is odd or $x$ is odd\" to just \"$x$ is odd.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$x$ is odd, or it is a prime number.\"\n\nFinally, we simplify the sentence to\n\n\"$x$ is odd or prime.\"",
